Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:41:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-47: several selected -- the fields whose values
 differ are shown empty, like WPF (0.47.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With a multi-selection the properties panel showed the primary's values,
which reads as "they are all 14px". WPF shows a field empty when the
selected controls do not agree (a checkbox half set). Now so does ours:
- host: after the panel data is built for a multi-selection, the page is
  asked for every selected one's layout / caption / look (lookAll), and
  lib/mixed.mixedFields marks the fields that differ (text compared
  case-blind; a control without the field does not count)
- panel: those fields are empty with the placeholder （不同）, a checkbox is
  indeterminate, a colour says （不同）; the row's name is italic, and it is
  not compared with the DFM there (no diff mark, no reset). Typing a value
  still sets it on all of them (R30).

Tests: lib (mixedFields), smoke (the panel data gets mixed = left / bold from
the page's answer), panels_render (Font.Size / Left empty, Font.Bold half
set and not a DFM difference, Top as it is), real VS Code (sbtExit + spbSave:
left / top / width / height / caption differ, the font size does not).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
